---
layout: base.njk
title: Capabilities
description: "Technical and enterprise SEO, local and multi-location search, analytics and attribution, content strategy, and workflow automation."
permalink: /capabilities/
sitemapPriority: 0.8
---

<section class="page-head">
  <div class="wrap">
    <p class="page-head__eyebrow">Capabilities</p>
    <h1>What I can own for a portfolio of accounts.</h1>
    <p class="lede" style="margin-top:var(--space-m)">
      Five areas, listed specifically enough that you can tell whether I've
      actually done the thing.
    </p>
  </div>
</section>

<section class="section section--flush">
  <div class="wrap">
    {%- for area in capabilities.areas %}
    <div id="{{ area.slug }}" style="margin-bottom:var(--space-2xl)">
      <h2>{{ area.title }}</h2>
      <p class="lede" style="margin-top:var(--space-s)">{{ area.summary }}</p>
      <ul class="checklist" style="margin-top:var(--space-m)">
        {%- for item in area.items %}
        <li>{{ item }}</li>
        {%- endfor %}
      </ul>
    </div>
    {%- endfor %}
  </div>
</section>

<section class="section section--alt">
  <div class="wrap stack">
    <h2>Tools</h2>
    <ul class="tags">
      {%- for tool in capabilities.tools %}
      <li class="tag">{{ tool }}</li>
      {%- endfor %}
    </ul>
    <p class="muted">
      Tools matter less than the reasoning behind their use, but it's a fair
      question, so here's the honest list of what I work in regularly.
    </p>
    <div class="actions">
      <a class="btn btn--primary" href="/case-studies/">See it applied</a>
      <a class="btn btn--ghost" href="/approach/">How I prioritize</a>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>
